title: Global options
tags: [[Command line]]
kind: reference
summary: -n / -u pick the repository, -p the daemon's port, --no-config ignores your settings — before the command, with environment fallbacks.

The repository and the daemon are chosen ''once'', by options that precede the
command, never per command:

|!Option |!Environment |!Selects |
|`-n <name>` |`METAFOLDER_REPO_NAME` |the loaded repository of that name |
|`-u <uuid>` |`METAFOLDER_REPO` |the loaded repository of that uuid |
|`-p <port>` |`METAFOLDER_DAEMON_PORT` |the daemon's port on `127.0.0.1` (default 7523) |
|`--no-config` | |ignore `cli/config.toml` entirely ([[CLI configuration]]) |

`-n` and `-u` are mutually exclusive. Names are unique among loaded repositories
— the daemon refuses to load a second one with the same name — so `-n` always
names one. The daemon listens on loopback only, so a port fully addresses it:
there is no URL option.

For every setting: an explicit option or environment variable, then the
configuration file (its default `[repo]`, its `daemon-port`), then the built-in
default. A command that needs a repository and gets none fails at once with a
usage error (exit code 2), without calling the daemon. The daemon-wide commands
(`mf repo`, `mf task`) ignore `-n`/`-u`, except `mf repo unload`, whose target they
name.

Because they are not options of the subcommands, they appear in `mf --help` only,
not in every command's help.
